From: Toemmsen96 <147745097+Toemmsen96@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6apm: voice call front end

Voice calls on AudioReach run entirely on the ADSP: the modem exchanges
voice packets with it, VCPM (the voice call proxy manager) runs the voice
graphs. Linux has to open those graphs, give VCPM its parameters and
calibration, and start them, connected to the Linux speaker and
microphone backends. The topology cannot describe them (VSID subgraph
property, control links, arbitrary ports, VCPM parameters and
out-of-band calibration at open).

This adds a "Voice Call Switch" control when the q6apm node has a
firmware-name: a file with the DSP command sequence (start and stop
commands, shared-memory blobs such as the VCPM calibration tables, and
the backend subgraphs the graphs need), built from the device's
calibration database. With the switch on, the start sequence runs once
all those backend subgraphs run (a playback and capture stream keep them
up during a call); before one of them stops, or when the switch goes
off, the stop sequence runs. q6apm_graph_start/stop keep count of the
running subgraphs for this. Commands go through the raw path of 0040,
out-of-band payloads through the shared memory of 0041.
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
@@ -5,6 +5,9 @@
